  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Borosilicate glasses contains B and sometimes Al. It can withstand heat changes without cracking. Such glasses are widely used for making good quality laboratory equipments. This glass has low coefficient of expansion.<br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Calcium-alkali-silicate glass is made by heating alkali metal carbonate, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> . This glass is used as domestic glass for windows and bottles.<br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Most of CaO can be replaced by PbO giving lead glass, which has higher reflective index and is used for making optical parts (lenses) and glass ornaments.<br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Soda glass is obtained by heating <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> , <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> . It is used for cheap laboratory glass wares."
